<description>
Dock two-tone sprites into color-matched horizontal bars with a color swap.

Input structure:
- bg = most common color.
- Top area: small two-tone sprites (outer color + inner color).
- Below: horizontal bars spanning most of the row, each with a fill color and border color on edges.

Rule:
- Match each sprite to the bar whose fill color equals the sprite's outer color.
- Place the sprite at its original x-position, aligned to the bar's bottom.
- Recolor: sprite outer → bar border, sprite inner → bar fill.
- Erase original sprites from the top area.

Key insight: Color matching is inverted — the sprite's dominant color identifies its target bar, then gets swapped to the bar's accent color.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "two-tone sprite s (outer color + inner color)",
  "dst": "dock into horizontal bar sprite d (fill + border)",
  "match_cond": "s.outer_color == d.fill_color",
  "transform": "place at same x near bottom of d; swap: s.outer→d.border, s.inner→d.fill"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 30x24, bg = most common color
  bars:
    count: 2-3 full-width horizontal bars in bottom portion
    structure: each row has border_color at cols 0 and W-1, fill_color at cols 1..W-2
    height: 4-8 rows per bar
    gap: exactly 1 bg row between consecutive bars
    colors: each bar has unique fill_color and unique border_color; fill != border; all fill colors distinct across bars
    border_color: may equal another bar's fill_color [observed]
  sprites:
    location: top area (above first bar), separated by bg
    count: 2-3 visual sprites (connected non-bg components)
    size: 2x2 to 5x9; height 2-5, width 2-9
    colors: 1-2 non-bg colors per sprite; all sprite colors are bar fill colors
    structure: outer_color (majority) wraps inner_color (minority, optional); may have bg holes
    symmetry: LR-symmetric [observed]
    matching: sprite outer_color == target bar's fill_color; 1-2 sprites per bar, 0 sprites for some bars allowed
    fit: sprite height <= target bar height; sprite x-range within cols 1..W-2
    no_x_overlap: sprites sharing same target bar must not overlap horizontally
  transform:
    erase: clear all sprites from top area (fill with bg)
    place: bottom-align each sprite within its matched bar at original x-position
    recolor: outer_color -> bar's border_color; inner_color -> bar's fill_color
    sub_sprites: solver also detects per-color connected components; inner-color sub-regions independently match/dock to their corresponding bar

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick bg, choose 2-3 bars with distinct (fill, border) color pairs; all fills distinct
    2. Stack bars bottom-up in grid rows 30x24 with 1-row bg gaps between them
    3. Design 2-3 small sprites using only bar fill colors (outer=fill_A, optional inner=fill_B)
    4. Ensure each sprite fits (height <= target bar height, x within cols 1..W-2, no x-overlap for co-targeted sprites)
    5. Build output: place color-swapped sprites bottom-aligned in their target bars
    6. Build input: erase sprites from bars, place original-color sprites in top area at same x-positions
```
